{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#851","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#851","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#851\",\"parent_revision\":\"24bbd8bf50f5af3833ca84450b738802ebdd3cd300a86a9a17e7db226d004d96\",\"root_revision\":\"24bbd8bf50f5af3833ca84450b738802ebdd3cd300a86a9a17e7db226d004d96\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nVerify that the bundled backlog MCP server starts correctly when the dh plugin is installed on a project that has no pre-existing backlog_core workspace entry. The .mcp.json uses ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} \u2014 this must be validated outside the development repo.\\n\\nTest steps:\\n1. Use a separate repo with no .claude/skills/backlog/ and no uv workspace entry for backlog_core\\n2. Install the dh plugin via /plugin install\\n3. Verify mcp__backlog__* tools appear in the session\\n4. Call backlog_list and confirm it returns successfully\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | dh plugin available in marketplace | AVAILABLE | `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` |\\n| 2 | A separate test repo available on the same machine | MISSING | Requires user to have a secondary repo |\\n| 3 | `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` resolves correctly in .mcp.json when installed | DERIVABLE | Check `.mcp.json` substitution behavior in Claude Code docs |\\n\\nVerdict: BLOCKED \u2014 requires a separate repo not under the current workspace. User must provide the test environment.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Validation task only, no code changes. Low risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Test conducted in a separate repo with no `.claude/skills/backlog/` and no uv workspace entry for backlog_core\\n- dh plugin installed via `/plugin install`\\n- `mcp__backlog__*` tools appear in the session\\n- `backlog_list` call returns successfully (not an error or timeout)\\n- Test results documented in a `.tmp/scratch/reports/` file noting environment, steps, and outcome\\n- Any failures produce a follow-up backlog item with the root cause and fix required\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.mcp.json` \u2014 under test (read-only verification)\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/` \u2014 test result documentation\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a development-harness plugin user, I need to verify that the bundled backlog MCP server starts correctly in a standalone repo (no pre-existing backlog_core workspace) so I can trust the plugin works outside the development environment.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **test: validate dh plugin mcp server in standalone repo** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4bb69750d1f9314fb976bb8ebb18c85bc531d6956bf2c8ff8e22e7d95aff2cb9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEcXg\"}"}